     1	//! Rust translation of `c_src/src/lib.c` (base64 decoder).
     2	//!
     3	//! The behaviour — including quirks of the original implementation — is
     4	//! reproduced exactly, so that the same input yields byte-identical output.
     5	//!
     6	//! The returned buffer is allocated with the C allocator (`calloc`) because the
     7	//! caller is expected to release it with `free()`.
