Comparison is over the [1mentire destination allocation[22m ([38;5;10mstrlen(src) + 14[0m bytes, matching the C [38;5;10mcalloc(sizeof(char), l + 13)[0m), not just the NUL-terminated prefix, so trailing zero-fill is checked too. Both buffers are then released with libc [38;5;10mfree[0m, which exercises the requirement that the Rust return value is C-allocator-owned.[0m[0m
