[38;5;10mcargo test[0m compiles the lib as a unit-test target but does [1mnot[22m refresh the [38;5;10mcdylib[0m artifact, because [38;5;10mcrate-type = ["cdylib"][0m gives integration tests no dependency edge to it. My first passing run was loading a stale [38;5;10m.so[0m. I caught this by injecting a deliberate mutation and seeing the tests still pass. The fix is [38;5;10mensure_cdylib_fresh()[0m in the harness, which shells out to [38;5;10mcargo build --lib[0m once per test binary with the matching profile and feature set.[0m[0m
