After that fix I ran a 16-mutant sweep over [38;5;10mdecode[0m's offsets and fallthrough, [38;5;10mis_base64[0m's accepted set, all three byte-assembly expressions, both [38;5;10m'='[0m checks, the allocation size, the group bounds, the loop stride, the [38;5;10mc2[0m/[38;5;10mc3[0m defaults, and the empty-string early return. All 16 were detected. Two of them abort the harness rather than failing an assertion (Rust [38;5;10mVec[0m bounds-check where C reads out of bounds), which my first detection heuristic misread as survival — that was a flaw in the mutation script, not in the tests.[0m[0m
